20,21 $ Not completely as above.(not : Cap 2-4 cm across, wrinkled and veined, greenish gray when young, becoming cinnamon gray; stem pale yellow; spores 7-9 x 5.5-6.5 µ)
21,0 $ Cap greenish yellow (sometimes with grayish or olive shades mixed in); gills yellowish to olive at first. $ Pluteus rugosidiscus
21,0 $ Cap olive brown to yellowish over the center, elsewhere brown; gills white at first, then yellowish before maturity. $ Pluteus lutescens
22,23 $ Cap white or whitish overall--or with a few brown fibers over a white ground color.
