50,51 $ Cap conspicuously and densely velvety or granular.
50,52 $ Cap not velvety or granular, or merely finely so.
51,0 $ Cap brownish with conspicuous, dark gray, reticulated wrinkles over the center; probably tropical and subtropical in distribution (recorded from Jamaica); poorly documented species based on a 1911 type collection that has been virtually destroyed by mold. $ Pluteus reticulatus
51,0 $ Cap uniformly dark brown, without wrinkles; widely distributed; well documented species. $ Pluteus granularis
52,0 $ Cap to 18 cm or more across, wrinkled; stem to 3 cm in diameter. $ Pluteus magnus
